    "title": "Special Weather Statement by NWS - NewsBreak",
    "text": "Check NWS updates here At 817 PM PDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm near Deer Park, or 18 miles north of Spokane, moving north at 10 mph. HAZARD...Winds in excess of 30 mph and penny size hail. SOURCE...Radar indicated. IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around unsecured objects. Minor hail damage to outdoor objects is possible. Locations impacted include... Deer Park, Clayton, and Tum Tum. This includes U.S. Highway 395 in Washington between mile markers 178 and 190.",
